Active PG primary can change without peering
Link: https://chatgpt.com/codex/cloud/security/findings/f4ea71fb47808191b0d12d944711138b?sev=&repo=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fjustincormack%2Fargmin
Criticality: informational (attack path: ignore)
Status: fixed

# Resolution
Fixed in commit `4d6ca72c Bind active PGs to peered primary`.

The finding was valid as a Phase 11 control-plane correctness defect. `Active`
PG records now persist the primary that completed peering in the version 6
control-plane state format. Serving and PG-operation authorization use that
bound primary instead of dynamically reselecting from the acting set, and
returning a PG to `Peering` clears the binding. `complete_pg_peering()` is
idempotent only for the already-bound active primary and only consults dynamic
deterministic primary selection for the `Peering` to `Active` transition. The
fix includes a regression where another acting-set member heartbeats first in
the active epoch but cannot become the serving primary or re-complete peering
while the PG remains active.

