## Rationale
Downgraded from high to ignore for current security triage. The validation evidence strongly supports a real control-plane correctness bug, but it is not reachable from the main argmin-s3 S3 HTTP service or current storage-node RPC path. Static evidence shows complete_pg_peering/serving_pg_primary are confined to crates/storage/src/control_plane.rs and tests, while current runtime construction uses static LocalPgRoute primary_node_id and configured Unix storage-node socket clients. A high rating would require a demonstrated in-scope attacker path to trigger the unsafe primary selection and route real writes through it; that path is absent in repository artifacts.
## Likelihood
ignore - Exploitation from the current threat-model surface is not realistic: public S3 clients cannot call the API, storage-node runtime routing is static/configured, and using the bug requires future integration plus an internal node/control-plane actor able to influence heartbeat/epoch ordering.
## Impact
ignore - If the new control-plane API were wired into multihost write routing, the impact could be high for integrity and availability because writes could be routed to a primary that did not complete peering. In the current repository runtime, no product path reaches this API, so there is no demonstrated security impact for deployed argmin-s3.
## Assumptions
- Assessment is limited to repository artifacts in /workspace/argmin; no cloud APIs were called and no deployment/IaC manifests were found.
- The main deployable product is the argmin-s3 binary and its S3 HTTP/storage-node runtime paths.
- The in-scope attacker for the project threat model is primarily an S3 client or an actor able to reach configured service endpoints, not an arbitrary Rust library consumer executing inside the process.
- The unfinished SingleAuthorityControlPlane API must be wired into runtime routing for writes or metadata mutations.
- An internal node/control-plane caller must be able to influence peering completion, heartbeat ordering, or epoch-changing heartbeats.
- The frontend/storage routing layer must trust serving_pg_primary for active PG write routing.
## Path
